OL,3,GNEWSARed Arrows to take to skies for
OL,4,ATour of Britain
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe Red Arrows will stage a flypast as
OL,7,Fpart of the 2026 Men's Tour of Britain
OL,8,Fcycle race.
OL,10,FThe RAF aerobatic team will soar over
OL,11,Friders at the start of stage two of the
OL,12,Frace in Boston, Lincolnshire on
OL,13,FThursday, while a Spitfire will fly
OL,14,Fover Skegness when the competitors
OL,15,Freach the finish line later that day.
OL,17,FDale Broughton, leader of Boston
OL,18,FBorough Council, said: "These flypasts
OL,19,Fwill provide a powerful tribute from
OL,20,Fthe skies in honour of an international
OL,21,Fclass of cyclists."
OL,23,APub: 01-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
